  "id": "1287cd16-803d-5b5c-b361-85f2429fa4a2",
  "slug": "easy-spaghetti-carbonara-recipe-11998102",
  "name": "Easy Spaghetti Carbonara",
  "recipe_type": "main",
  "brief_description": "Spaghetti Carbonara is the ultimate easy-cooking comfort food. Follow this recipe for perfecting the simple yet rich dish and its trademark silky, smooth sauce.",
  "cuisine": "Italian",
  "instructions": [
    {
      "position": 1,
      "text": "Whisk together eggs and Pecorino Romano in a medium bowl."
    },
    {
      "position": 2,
      "text": "Cook pancetta in a large skillet over medium heat, stirring often, until evenly browned, about 10 minutes."
    },
    {
      "position": 3,
      "text": "Meanwhile, bring a large pot of salted water to a boil. Cook spaghetti according to package directions, reserving 2\u20443 cup pasta cooking water. Drain; add spaghetti to pancetta in skillet. Remove skillet from heat."
    },
    {
      "position": 4,
      "text": "Stir 1\u20444 cup pasta water into egg mixture to temper eggs. Add egg mixture to spaghetti in skillet; stir constantly, adding enough pasta cooking water to reach desired consistency, until spaghetti is coated and eggs are just set but not curdled. Garnish with black pepper and/or additional Pecorino Romano. Note: Guanciale is the traditional cured pork choice for carbonara. It has a high fat-to-meat ratio, which contributes to a silky end product. But it can be hard to find and expensive. So use pancetta instead. Bacon can be used in a pinch, too. Pecorino Romano is aged sheep\u2019s-milk cheese with a sharp and salty flavor. For the best texture, grate your own. But you can substitute Parmesan, no problem."
    }
  ],
  "servings": 4,
  "cooking_time_minutes": null,
  "preparation_time_minutes": 10,
  "rest_time_minutes": null,
